    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0875" n="863" xml:id="pg863"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Japan)/11–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-21T13:00:00-05:00">November 21,
                            1945—1 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2374. Final paragraph your 3903, Nov. 20. For your information and use in your
                    discretion, Commanding General China Theater reported on 10 Nov that due to
                    unsettled conditions in China it would not be possible to send Chinese
                    occupational forces to Japan for several months and that “the Gimo<anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d618-f1"/> regrets very much inability to participate and will do so
                    should local situation clarify”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d618-f1" n="34" xml:id="d618-f1-content">
                <p>Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
